                    sling:resourceType="wcm/foundation/components/text"
                    text="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;>&lt;b>The following applies to all types of appeals&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;ol>&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Appeal Cover sheet must be complete and signed.&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Provide a written statement that clearly and concisely states the appeal reason.&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Provide official transcripts and/or test scores, (e.g. AP or SAT subject – if applicable to satisfy a subject.&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Include all supporting documentation with your appeal, (e.g., proof of mailing/submission of requested information, medical/legal documentation), as applicable.&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Only one appeal may be submitted per semester. Appeal decisions are final.&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Applicants will be notified approximately 3-4 weeks after submission of a complete appeal packet of a decision and will be reflected on your Student Center.&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;All appeals must be received within 30-Days from the “missed deadline” or “deny” notification from the Office of Admissions.&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;/ol>&#xa;"
                    textIsRich="true">
